#: ../smart-base/L1/processes/classify-and-code-content.bpmn:29
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Classifies and codes L1 extracted statements (recommendations, implementation practices, remarks, proposed coverage exclusions) and L2 DAK slots (personas, business processes, guideline domains, conditions, interventions, medicines, GRADE ratings), following the terminology-coding methodology and the classify-and-code-content skill. The authoring agent runs terminology-lookup down the four-rung reuse-first ladder, records provenance (declared, context, inferred) and candidate status, and stages the result. A person in the l1-extraction-reviewer lane signs or rejects each exclusion proposed in exclusions.proposed.json against the printed page (sections/page-NNN.md). A person in the terminologist / ontologist lane then adjudicates the candidate codings, SKOS match precision (exactMatch vs closeMatch) and any Rung 4 local glossary candidates."
msgstr ""

